From 8b705bed0f407965d6436bc1da219f5ad2363935 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Payton <brandon@happycode.net>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:29:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 18/22] regexp/syntax: Reuse traversal storage and retain
 equivalence tests

Keep one iterative compiler on every target. Shallow expressions use an
inline buffer; deeper expressions borrow cleared scratch storage without
making the inline array escape. Drop exceptionally large buffers instead
of retaining them in the pool.

Retain the original traversal only as a test oracle, compare full programs
for fixed and generated expressions, exercise concurrent reuse and add
compilation-only benchmarks. Stack safety is the purpose; benchmark
results do not establish a universal compilation speed improvement.

